# UBSan suppressions for run.sh --asan. Only the vendored LZ *encoder* is listed: its hash (spice-common
# lz_compress_tmpl.c, HASH_FUNC) shifts and adds signed ints that overflow. It is upstream code that builds the
# test inputs here and is not used by the viewer. Nothing in the decoders is suppressed.
signed-integer-overflow:lz_compress_tmpl.c
shift-base:lz_compress_tmpl.c
